{
    "background_story": "Augustus was a sailor with a reputation for being, well, less than stellar at his job. Despite his best efforts, he always seemed to find a way to get himself and his crew into trouble. His lack of seamanship was the stuff of legend, with tales of him getting seasick on calm waters and accidentally steering the ship into the dock. One infamous incident involved Augustus attempting to tie a simple knot, only to end up with a tangled mess that took hours to untangle. His crewmates often joked that Augustus was the only sailor they knew who could get lost on a ship with a GPS system. Despite his unseamanlike tendencies, Augustus was a lovable and well-meaning soul, and his crewmates tolerated his antics out of affection for the hapless sailor.",
